0008: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0009:     """
0010:     Complete a grid of colored blocks to match a minimap legend in the top-left corner.
0011: 
0012:     Input structure:
0013:     - bg = most common color.
0014:     - Top-left corner: a small sprite of single colored pixels forming a minimap pattern on a regular lattice.
0015:     - Main area: uniformly colored square blocks (NxN) arranged on a regular grid; some positions are empty (bg).
0016: 
0017:     Rule:
0018:     - The legend pixels define a color pattern; each pixel's lattice position maps to a block position in the main grid via a fixed scale factor and offset.
0019:     - Existing colored blocks confirm the scale/offset alignment.
0020:     - For every legend pixel whose corresponding grid position is empty, place a new block of that color.
0021: 
0022:     Key insight: The top-left pixel pattern is a scaled-down minimap of the block layout; the mapping is inferred from blocks already present.
0023:     """
