/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:711:#    Each rectangle has its own background color, and all sprites plus anchors stay
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:713:#    a top/bottom anchor means horizontal sliding, and a left/right anchor means
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:714:#    vertical sliding. The crucial new twist is that anchor colors can repeat across
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:715:#    the two rectangles, so color alone no longer selects the destination anchor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:716:#    Small example: if both the left and right halves each contain a border anchor
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:718:#    anchor, while another sprite with marker 4 in the right half must align to the
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:719:#    right-half anchor. The original logic would collapse both into one global
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:720:#    color→anchor map; the variant requires region→(color→anchor).
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/tem3/combo_prompt_581f7754_19.txt:733:#    - Matching by `anchors_by_color[color]` is no longer valid because the same
